# Docker Guidelines

- Use a minimal, pinned base image and rebuild it regularly for security updates.
- Use multi-stage builds so build tools and source files do not reach the runtime image.
- Copy dependency manifests before application source to make dependency-install layers cacheable.
- Run the service as a non-root user and grant it only the filesystem permissions it needs.
- Keep build context small with a `.dockerignore`; never copy credentials, local environments, or build output into an image.
- Prefer explicit image tags or digests and make build inputs reproducible.
- Add a health check when the service has a meaningful readiness endpoint.
